Biochemical conversion of corn stover to ethanol — Humbird and colleagues (@ic-biorefinery: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_123G817BYJFAVYGA0ZVK3J5FJH
D. Humbird and colleagues. Process Design and Economics for Biochemical Conversion of Lignocellulosic Biomass to Ethanol: Dilute-Acid Pretreatment and Enzymatic Hydrolysis of Corn Stover. NREL/TP-5100-47764, 2011. [Laboratory record](https://research-hub.nlr.gov/en/publications/process-design-and-economics-for-biochemical-conversion-of-lignoc/) · [Authorized full report](https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy11osti/47764.pdf).

Read the entire design report: feed and conversion assumptions, pretreatment, enzymatic hydrolysis/fermentation, recovery, wastewater, utilities, material/energy accounts, equipment/cost basis and sensitivity. Independently reconstruct consequential results and compare a changed feed, yield or energy boundary. A publicly inspectable conceptual design is distinct from measurements of a fully operating commercial plant.

The title, authorship, report number, date, scope and official full-text route were verified on 29 October 2026. The original laboratory identity remains NREL in the citation; its current repository/file hosts use nlr.gov. Direct PDF retrieval timed out through the browser, so full-page inspection is not claimed. Preserve report/contract and component notices and dated cost assumptions. Nothing is mirrored or executed.

